## Test Smell Audit — testsmells.org 19-Smell Catalog

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.x · .NET 10 · `[TestCategory("Integration")]`  
**Calibration:** Integration-test norms applied (Mystery Guest / Eager Test downgraded for hermetic in-memory SQLite)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 0           | 0              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **3**       | **3**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 1. Sleepy Test — HIGH

**Smell:** Test waits via `Thread.Sleep` instead of an event-driven mechanism.  
**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← arbitrary 3-second wall-clock wait
```

**Why it matters (even in integration tests):** Adds 3 s of dead time per run, and if the notification system is slow on CI the test becomes flaky. Integration-test calibration does *not* exempt hard sleeps — only real async waits.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Poll or use a retry helper with timeout
await AsyncAssert.EventuallyAsync(
    () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
    timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
```

---

#### 2. Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**Smell:** `if`/`else` changes which assertion executes; one branch is never verified for each run.  
**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Why it matters:** Test data creates a standard `User`, so the `PremiumUser` branch is dead code — silently never exercised.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

#### 3. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**Smell:** Test exercises code but never asserts an outcome — passes as long as no exception is thrown.  
**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← nothing verified
```

**Why it matters:** A broken `Insert` that silently discards rows would still pass this test.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    Assert.AreEqual(100, _repository.ListAll().Count);
}
```

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✓

The remaining 5 tests are well-designed:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|--------------|
| `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | Clear arrange-act-assert, multiple facets verified |
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Focused, asserts the mutation |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Asserts absence with `Assert.IsNull` |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is self-documenting (3 items just added) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Tests concurrency, asserts final state |

The shared `[TestInitialize]` fixture is appropriate — every test uses both `_connection` and `_repository` (no General Fixture smell). The in-memory SQLite approach avoids Mystery Guest entirely.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~1 min | Eliminates false confidence |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Removes dead-code branch, adds missing coverage |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~15 min | Removes 3 s latency + flakiness risk (may need a polling helper) |

**Bottom line:** 5 of 8 tests (63 %) are clean. The 3 smells are all High-severity but straightforward to fix — the biggest win is adding one assertion to `BulkInsert` (one line, immediate payoff).
